𒑰 DUB.SAR 1.0 Example: Geometric Inclination and Direction
𒑰 Difficulty: Advanced
𒑰 Concept: Directions, Turns & Rotations
𒑰 Mode: Mixed (Cuneiform syntax with Latin identifiers)
𒑰
𒑰 Purpose:
𒑰   Computes canal and ramp inclinations (rise/run) and feeds (run/rise),
𒑰   constructs directed quantities, and executes turn rotations.
𒑰
𒑰 Expected Output:
𒑰   0;20
𒑰   3
𒑰   0;30
𒑰   2
𒑰   direction(quarter-turn)
𒑰   direction(0;22,30-turn)
𒑰   10 meter along direction(quarter-turn)

𒂊𒁹

    𒑰 1. Consult Old Babylonian ramp inclinations from the Tablet Archive (BM 85194)
    ramp_info : take "standard-ramp" from "inclinations"
    hist_inc : ramp_info.inclination
    hist_feed : ramp_info.feed

    𒑰 2. Form an inclination determination from rise and run
    𒑰 1 rise, 2 run (steep ramp)
    slope : 1 2 inclination
    inc : slope.inclination
    fd : slope.feed

    𒑰 3. Form a direction from a turn fraction and rotate by an eighth-turn
    base_dir : quarter-turn direction
    rotated_dir : base_dir eighth-turn rotate

    𒑰 4. Construct a directed quantity and rotate it
    force : 10 meter quarter-turn rotate

𒅗𒁹

    𒁹𒀀 hist_inc
    𒁹𒀀 hist_feed
    𒁹𒀀 inc
    𒁹𒀀 fd
    𒁹𒀀 base_dir
    𒁹𒀀 rotated_dir
    𒁹𒀀 force
